The tapi command against LLVM 21, and its --no-compact option.

libtapi builds with the scripts and the first two patches; the command and
the libraries only it uses do not.  LLVM 21's option tables are written by
TableGen with more fields than tapi's OPTION macro took, so the driver
uses LLVM_MAKE_OPT_ID and LLVM_CONSTRUCT_OPT_INFO as LLVM's own tools do.
clang's DiagnosticOptions is no longer reference-counted and is passed by
reference; FileManager hands out FileEntryRef and DirectoryEntryRef rather
than pointers; the thunk manglers take the elide-override flag; clang's AST
dropped MemberPointerType::getClass and the dependent-template accessors,
which the structural-equivalence copy now reaches the way clang's does;
CompilerInstance takes its invocation at construction; endianness moved to
llvm::endianness; InterfaceFile::addRPath takes the path first.

--no-compact is Apple's: tapi-2100 writes TBD v5 JSON compact unless asked
not to, and has the option on archive, stubify and installapi.  This tapi
predates it and always pretty-printed, so the writer takes the choice and
the default follows Apple's.

